Fall back to a loaded font that has the character before the default font file.

ass_font_select looks for a character in the style's family, then the default family, then asks the
default provider for a fallback family, then hands back the default font file without checking it.
Only a system provider can answer the fallback, and fonts added with ass_add_font or read from the
fonts directory belong to no provider that has one, so they never take part in it. A build without
a system provider, as on Android, Linux without fontconfig and the web, therefore draws a box for
every character the style's font and the default family lack, even when another loaded font has
it, and that is how Chinese, Japanese, Korean, Thai and Arabic lines in a script naming a font the
device lacks turn into boxes. Where a provider exists, the same fonts are still never tried.

After the provider's fallback fails, and before the default font file, ass_font_select now takes
the first font in loading order whose provider has no fallback of its own and which has the
character, and selects the best match for the style's weight and slant inside that font's family
that also has it, the way a provider's fallback family is used. It runs only for a real character,
never for the first face a style opens, so the font a style starts from does not change, and a
provider's own fonts are not searched a second time.

Applied by BuildAssChainTask and BuildAssChainWasmTask before configure.

diff --git a/libass/ass_fontselect.c b/libass/ass_fontselect.c
index 2303876..e2b0607 100644
--- a/libass/ass_fontselect.c
+++ b/libass/ass_fontselect.c
@@ -871,6 +871,43 @@ static char *select_font(ASS_FontSelector *priv,
 }
 
 
+/**
+ * \brief Find a font for a character that the style's family, the default
+ * family and the default provider's own fallback all lack, among the fonts
+ * no fallback search covers: those of a provider without get_fallback, in
+ * practice the fonts added with ass_add_font or read from the fonts dir.
+ * The first such font in loading order that has the character names the
+ * family, and the best match for the style inside that family which also
+ * has it is selected, the way a provider's fallback family is used.
+ */
+static char *select_loaded_fallback(ASS_FontSelector *priv,
+                                    unsigned bold, unsigned italic,
+                                    int *index, char **postscript_name,
+                                    int *uid, ASS_FontStream *stream,
+                                    uint32_t code)
+{
+    for (int x = 0; x < priv->n_font; x++) {
+        ASS_FontInfo *font = &priv->font_infos[x];
+        if (font->provider->funcs.get_fallback || !font->n_family)
+            continue;
+        if (!check_glyph(font, code))
+            continue;
+
+        char *family = font->families[0];
+        ASS_FontProviderMetaData meta = {
+            .n_fullname = 1,
+            .fullnames  = &family,
+        };
+        bool name_match = false;
+        char *res = find_font(priv, meta, false, bold, italic, index,
+                              postscript_name, uid, stream, code, &name_match);
+        if (res)
+            return res;
+    }
+
+    return NULL;
+}
+
 /**
  * \brief Find a font. Use default family or path if necessary.
  * \param family font family
@@ -919,6 +956,16 @@ char *ass_font_select(ASS_FontSelector *priv,
         }
     }
 
